From: Sobs <antohasobne@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] client: bare_app: a USB keyboard and mouse as they are

bare_app sends a game started with a keyboard and a mouse (Heroes III)
the keys of a USB keyboard as Linux key codes (GAME_MSG_KEY) and a USB
mouse's buttons and moves (GAME_MSG_MOUSE_*). The link makes SDL's
events of them, so VCMI's own keyboard and mouse handling drives the
game, its hotkeys included:

- keys: SDL key events (the Linux codes mapped to SDL scancodes), and
  while a text input waits, the characters they type on a US layout as
  SDL text input. SDL's keyboard state does not see events pushed this
  way, so the modifiers held come from the link (ctrlDown, shiftDown,
  altDown) in InputHandler and InputSourceKeyboard. Once a USB keyboard
  has been used, text inputs take its keys instead of opening the
  on-screen keyboard.
- the mouse: one SDL motion per poll, the counts as screen pixels from
  where the cursor is (the stick moves it too; VCMI keeps its own
  position while a button drags, so the link keeps the mouse's), presses
  at the cursor with double clicks counted as SDL does (500 ms, 4 px),
  the wheel. A move brings a magnifier the D-pad moved away back to the
  cursor, as the stick does.

